# Rip's names on Janus's edge. rip sites keeps this file in Janus's sites
# directory (rip.caddy), where the service Caddyfile imports it.
#
# via.rip and *.via.rip publicly resolve to 127.0.0.1: the apex carries the
# Rip status page (the agent registers its status socket under it) and the
# subdomains carry the apps. Every name is an app registered with Janus,
# and every certificate is an exact-host cert the local CA mints on demand
# for a registered name (browsers reject second-level wildcards). The LAN
# family, rip.local and *.local, is Janus's own *.local site; apps claim a
# .local twin for every .via.rip host and register both.
#
# Trust is Janus's: 'janus trust' on this machine, http://janus.local/trust
# on a phone. Reach is Janus's too ('janus mode'); the routing is the same
# in every mode.
via.rip, *.via.rip {
	tls {
		issuer internal
		on_demand
	}
	janus
	log {
		output stderr
		format janus
	}
}
